what do u mean by the localstorage ??
means is a feature of web browser that let browser saves your data directly on your device (in your browser)
so it can be used later--->even after you close and reopen  the browser

in simple words it puts build-in storage box for the website on your computer 


note localstorage is not fully sequire or save to handle data like password or credit card details 

what is the ddiff between the stringify and the parse() json
the diff between in this two is 
are two diff things but works oppositly 

stringify--->js objects--->json string

parse--->json string--->js objects

so the question is why do we need them ??
because the localstorage stores only in the string 
apis often sends the data in the json string 
so we convert object to string before storing/sending them 

        Quick Difference Table
Feature	    JSON.stringify()	  JSON.parse()
Converts    Object → String	      String → Object
Purpose	    Store/send data	      Read/use data
Output      TypeString	          Object 